  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan names the move icy drill stardust and calls it his unique creation. At full activation he can unleash a water vat sized starlight lump up to six times. The bigger the lump, the slower it moves, because more stardust inside means more collisions and more energy spent on speed.",
      "chapters": [
        670
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a spar with Tai Bai Yun Sheng, lumps explode into starlight specks that collide and burst with frost energy. Tai Bai Yun Sheng judges that Fang Yuan has not used fifty percent of the move’s power, and that the force already far surpasses most mortal killer moves though it cannot compare to an immortal killer move. Tai Bai Yun Sheng also values the move at least at four immortal essence stones in treasure yellow heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        670
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan fuses a brand new star Gu from Dou Min Jun’s inheritance that raises the attack power of star path Gu worms, which is why he chooses a star path attack method. Without Little Immortal Xing Luo’s icy yarn and six-nine stardust, he would not have been able to deduce icy drill stardust even with wisdom Gu. The finished move differs from icy stardust: smaller range, much greater power.",
      "chapters": [
        670
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
